# ICC freshness (motor DAC) — lesson 2026-07-20

## Symptom

AO square-waved mid↔command every ~100 ms while UART still showed correct stick µs.

## Cause

Staleness used **time since last take** (take cleared `valid`). If the CM4 loop missed takes for ~`CUST_ICC_MOTOR_DAC_MAX_AGE_MS`, CM4 forced mid even though the handler kept receiving packets and latched commands looked fine.

## Fix (keep)

1. **Peek** latest motor slot; do not clear on read for age purposes (`has_data` + `rx_tick_ms` on store).
2. Age = `now - slot.rx_tick_ms` (last **RX** in handler).
3. Motor max age **300 ms** (was 100; steer uses 500 ms) — both `cust_icc.h`.

## Rule

For cyclic Customer ICC commands: freshness = **last receive stamp**, not last consumer drain. Timeout ≫ send period and tolerant of CM4 load (Log15 / Log18 B+A).
